  "guidebook": {
    "intro": "Luganda questions keep the same word order as statements. The question word simply goes where the answer would be, usually at the end.",
    "phrases": [
      { "target": "Kino kiki?", "base": "What is this?" },
      { "target": "Ani oyo?", "base": "Who is that?" },
      { "target": "Oli wa kati?", "base": "Where are you now?" },
      { "target": "Ojja ddi?", "base": "When are you coming?" },
      { "target": "Lwaki osoma Oluganda?", "base": "Why are you learning Luganda?" },
      { "target": "Oyogera Oluganda?", "base": "Do you speak Luganda?" },
      { "target": "Kino kiyitibwa kitya mu Luganda?", "base": "What is this called in Luganda?" }
    ],
    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "question-words",
        "title": "The answer goes in the same place",
        "body": [
          "Ask **Ogenda wa?** (you-go where?) and answer **Ŋŋenda Jinja** (I-go Jinja). Swap the question word for the answer and the sentence is done.",
          "A yes/no question is a statement with a rising voice: **Oyogera Oluganda?** Add **oba** (or) to offer a choice: **Caayi oba kaawa?**"
        ],
        "table": [
          ["Word", "Meaning", "Example"],
          ["ki", "what", "Oyagala ki?"],
          ["ani", "who", "Ani oyo?"],
          ["wa", "where", "Oli wa?"],
          ["ddi", "when", "Ojja ddi?"],
          ["lwaki", "why", "Lwaki osoma?"],
          ["mmeka", "how many / how much", "Ssente mmeka?"]
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ask-about-words",
        "title": "Learning from people",
        "body": [
          "The best phrase for a learner: point and ask **Kino kiyitibwa kitya mu Luganda?** (What is this called in Luganda?). If you miss the answer, say **Ddamu mpola** (repeat slowly). People love helping a learner."
        ]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Njogera katono",
        "body": [
          "Answering **Njogera katono** (I speak a little) to **Oyogera Oluganda?** almost always gets a smile, and often a long conversation. Ugandans are proud when visitors try their language."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "what-is-this",
      "title": "What is this called?",
      "unlockAfter": "u18s3l3",
      "cast": ["emma", "jjajja"],
      "summary": "Emma asks Jjajja the names of things in her kitchen.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Jjajja, kino kiyitibwa kitya mu Luganda?", "base": "Grandma, what is this called in Luganda?" }
        },
        { "line": { "speaker": "jjajja", "target": "Ekyo kibbo.", "base": "That is a basket." }, "gloss": { "kibbo": "a basket" } },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Kibbo. Ate kino kiki?", "base": "Basket. And what is this?" },
          "gloss": { "Ate": "and, what about" }
        },
        { "line": { "speaker": "jjajja", "target": "Kino kyambe.", "base": "This is a knife." }, "gloss": { "kyambe": "a knife" } },
        { "question": "What is Emma doing?", "options": ["Asking the names of things", "Cooking dinner", "Buying a basket"], "answer": 0 },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Sitegeera. Ddamu mpola, Jjajja.", "base": "I don’t understand. Repeat slowly, Grandma." }
        },
        { "line": { "speaker": "jjajja", "target": "Ekyambe. Kino kyambe.", "base": "A knife. This is a knife." } },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "jjajja", "target": "Lwaki osoma Oluganda, mwana wange?", "base": "Why are you learning Luganda, my child?" }
        },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Kubanga njagala okwogera naawe!", "base": "Because I want to talk with you!" },
          "gloss": { "naawe": "with you" }
        },
        {
          "question": "Why is Emma learning Luganda?",
          "options": ["For school", "To talk with Jjajja", "To buy things at the market"],
          "answer": 1
        },
        {
          "line": { "speaker": "jjajja", "target": "Ayi, kirungi nnyo! Oyogera bulungi.", "base": "Oh, that’s very good! You speak well." }
        },
        { "line": { "speaker": "emma", "target": "Nedda, njogera katono.", "base": "No, I speak a little." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
